HST Office: a .docx with an endnote, once reopened and saved again, made Word save a .doc that Word
itself could not open ("Office has detected a problem with this file").

DocxAttributeOutput::WriteFootnoteEndnotePr() wrote <w:pos w:val="sectEnd"/> into <w:footnotePr>
and <w:endnotePr>, both in settings.xml and in every section's <w:sectPr>, whenever the first
section format collected endnotes at its end. After a .docx import that first format is the
node-less section the layout creates for continuous endnotes (SwEndNoteInfo::GetSwSection), so
every reopened document with an endnote got it. Word writes the endnote placement in settings.xml
only; with the placement in <w:sectPr> its .doc output cannot be reopened (reproduced with a .docx
made by Word itself), and "end of section" is not a footnote placement.

Now only settings.xml <w:endnotePr> gets the placement, taken from the first section that has
nodes. The .doc export (DOP epc) skips node-less sections the same way.

Test: tests/runtime/check-docx-word-interop.py (endnote and footnote placement after a round trip).
---
--- a/sw/source/filter/ww8/docxattributeoutput.cxx
+++ b/sw/source/filter/ww8/docxattributeoutput.cxx
@@ -9346,14 +9346,20 @@
 {
     fs->startElementNS(XML_w, tag);
 
-    SwSectionFormats& rSections = m_rExport.m_rDoc.GetSections();
-    if (!rSections.empty())
+    // HST Office: "end of section" is an endnote placement, and Word writes it in settings.xml
+    // only. With <w:pos w:val="sectEnd"/> in a section's <w:endnotePr>, Word saves a .doc that it
+    // then refuses to open; <w:footnotePr> got the endnote placement as well.
+    // Sections without nodes are skipped: the layout creates one ("Endnote", collect at end) for
+    // continuous endnotes, which is not a request to collect endnotes at the section end.
+    if (tag == XML_endnotePr && listtag != 0)
     {
-        SwSectionFormat* pFormat = rSections[0];
-        bool bEndnAtEnd = pFormat->GetEndAtTextEnd().IsAtEnd();
-        if (bEndnAtEnd)
+        for (const SwSectionFormat* pFormat : m_rExport.m_rDoc.GetSections())
         {
-            fs->singleElementNS(XML_w, XML_pos, FSNS(XML_w, XML_val), "sectEnd");
+            if (!pFormat->GetSectionNode())
+                continue;
+            if (pFormat->GetEndAtTextEnd().IsAtEnd())
+                fs->singleElementNS(XML_w, XML_pos, FSNS(XML_w, XML_val), "sectEnd");
+            break;
         }
     }
 
--- a/sw/source/filter/ww8/wrtww8.cxx
